{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>It is not in heaven.</b> It is possible to interpret that since this Torah was in heaven, it now says 'it is not in heaven' — for I have already brought it down to you from there; and the word היא alludes to the supernal wisdom that is in heaven." "<b>And it is not beyond the sea.</b> This is the Oceanus, which surrounds the entire inhabited world, where the supernal wisdom is; therefore it was necessary to mention 'sea,' for otherwise he should have mentioned the tehom and said 'it is not in the tehom,' as Job said (Job 28:14): ״תהום אמר לא בי היא״, and the account would have been more fitting to mention a way of ascent and a way of descent. And he mentioned the word היא for each and every matter, which is a term of restriction, and also to include the supernal comprehensive wisdom that encompasses all — it encompasses the spheres, and the spheres encompass the sea, and the sea encompasses the inhabited world; and this is what is said: ״לא נפלאת היא ממך״ and ״ולא רחוקה היא,״ to indicate that there is a wisdom that is far, and likewise ״לא בשמים היא״ and ״ולא מעבר לים היא.״ And further we may say that he mentioned the word היא four times, corresponding to the four supernal elements that are drawn and emanated from the supernal wisdom, and these are their names in allusion: Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and David; from them, corresponding to them, were emanated in the world of separate intelligences the four holy living creatures and the four ofannim, and in this lower world the four elements, which are the sustenance of every composite and its endurance." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״לא בשמים היא״ — it will not be found among the arrogant of spirit; ״ולא מעבר לים היא״ — it will not be found neither among traders nor among merchants. Samuel said: the Torah is found neither among stargazers nor among astrologers, as it is said ״לא בשמים היא״; the Torah is found only in one who engages in the work of heaven. They said to Samuel: but you yourself are an astrologer! He said to them: all my days I never looked at this wisdom except at the time when I went to relieve myself in the bathhouse — thus far. And about these wisdoms Isaiah would warn Israel, saying to them (Isaiah 55:2): ״למה תשקלו כסף בלוא לחם ויגיעכם בלוא לשבעה״ — he says to them: you weigh out silver and squander money to acquire wisdoms that are not bread, in which the soul is not nourished; or, why do you toil and waste your strength and consume your days on things from which your soul will not be satisfied? ״שמעו שמוע אלי ואכלו טוב״ — that is the Torah, which is called ״לקח טוב,״ for this is the true bread, and it shall be for you for satiation; and likewise ״ותתענג בדשן נפשכם״ — that is, in this bread your soul shall delight in the supernal radiance, just as the body delights in fatness; and so David said of the soul's delight (Psalms 63:6): ״כמו חלב ודשן תשבע נפשי.״ From here we learn that one should not engage in the other wisdoms but only in the essence, which is our Torah. Go out and learn from Samuel, who did not engage in them except in a place forbidden for speaking words of Torah — and it is an impure place; and likewise the Sages, of blessed memory, said: Go out and find an hour that is neither of the day nor of the night, and study Greek wisdom. And the reason is that through engaging in the other wisdoms a person may sometimes come in matters of faith to a deviation from the path of truth, for there is no wisdom in the world that does not contain dross and dregs; and therefore all the wisdoms are likened to silver, for silver mostly contains dregs and is not pure silver; but our Torah is silver that contains no dregs whatsoever, and therefore it is likened to refined silver, as it is written (Psalms 12:7): ״כסף צרוף בעליל לארץ מזוקק שבעתים.״" "<b><big>W</big>ho <big>w</big>ill go up <big>f</big>or us <big>t</big>o heaven.</b> There is an allusion here that the Unique Name — its attainment is possible only for the people Israel who are circumcised, for they are sealed with the sign of the holy covenant. And we also find that no one prophesies standing except one who is circumcised: thus we find in Abraham before the circumcision, concerning whom it is written (Genesis 17): ״ויפול על פניו״ — he did not prophesy but fell; after the circumcision, standing, as it is written (ibid. 18): ״ואברהם עודנו עומד לפני ה'.״ And Balaam never prophesied except falling, as it is said (Numbers 24:4): ״נופל וגלוי עינים.״ And likewise Moses alluded to this in what he said to the Holy One, blessed be He, at the bush (Exodus 3:13–14): ״ואמרו לי מה שמו מה אומר אליהם״ — he says that the circumcised will ask Him about the Unique Name." "<b>And because</b> the commandment is sealed with the sign of the holy covenant, therefore they said in the Midrash (Song of Songs 2:7): ״בצבאות או באילות השדה״ — a host (צבא) in which I have a sign (אות); and they did not say 'that it was for me a sign.' And Scripture alluded, in the Unique Name, to the circumcision of the flesh, after having explicitly mentioned the circumcision of the heart, saying above: ״ומל ה' אלהיך את לבבך וגו׳״ — for the circumcision of the heart is the annulment of the evil inclination, and when the evil inclination is annulled, all of a person's limbs are drawn and cleave to the Unique Name and perform naturally what reason requires. And the allusion comes in this section to indicate that in the time of redemption all Israel, who possess attainment, will be circumcised in heart and flesh, cleaving to the Unique Name; and this is the allusion of ״מי יעלה לנו השמימה.״ And likewise the prophet, peace be upon him, said (Jeremiah 31:33): ״כי כולם ידעו אותי למקטנם ועד גדולם.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:45.168109297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}